cargo-zempic 0.0.1
  workspace:      [WORKSPACE_ROOT]  (1 members, 1 selected)
  profile:        release  (inherits: none)
  optimizing for: size
  target:         aarch64-apple-darwin

── TIER 1 · FOUNDATIONAL ──────────────────────────────────────────── 2 findings

  ╭ HIGH  profile/strip                                                    large
  │ change    unset -> "symbols"
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix safe
  │ why       The symbol table and the strings it references are kept in the
  │           linked artifact even though they are not needed to run it.
  │ tradeoff  Stripping removes function names from backtraces and profiler
  ╰           output.

  ╭ MEDIUM  profile/missing-config                                      moderate
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none
  │ why       Every setting falls back to cargo's defaults, which favor compile
  │           time over a small artifact. The other findings in this report name
  │           the settings to set.
  ╰ tradeoff  There is nothing to lose by configuring the profile.

── TIER 2 · COMPILER ──────────────────────────────────────────────── 3 findings

  ╭ HIGH  profile/opt-level:size                                           large
  │ change    unset -> "z"
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime notable · fix consequential
  │ why       The compiler optimizes for speed. Optimizing for size lets it drop
  │           code that exists only to run faster.
  ╰ tradeoff  Runtime cost, pronounced with `"z"` on compute-heavy code.

  ╭ MEDIUM  profile/lto                                                 moderate
  │ change    unset -> "fat"
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix consequential
  │ why       Optimizing across crate boundaries removes code a per-crate build
  │           must keep.
  ╰ tradeoff  Link time rises substantially.

  ╭ LOW  profile/codegen-units                                        negligible
  │ change    unset -> 1
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix consequential
  │ why       A single code generation unit lets `profile/lto` optimize across
  │           the whole crate; with several units, that optimization is limited.
  │ tradeoff  Compiles are slower; the setting is what unlocks link-time
  ╰           optimization.

── TIER 3 · BEHAVIORAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────── 1 finding

  ╭ LOW  profile/panic-abort                                               small
  │ change    unset -> "abort"
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix consequential
  │ why       Unwinding carries the machinery that walks the stack and runs
  │           destructors. Aborting on panic lets the compiler drop it.
  │ tradeoff  Aborting loses unwinding: a `catch_unwind` in the workspace or any
  │           dependency will no longer recover from a panic. The setting
  ╰           applies workspace-wide, because `panic` cannot be set per package.

SUMMARY
  6 findings: 2 high, 2 medium, 2 low.  By magnitude: 2 large, 2 moderate, 1 small, 1 negligible.
  5 auto-fixable.

  Magnitude is an ordinal judgement, not a measurement. zempic does not build
  and does not read compiled artifacts, so it reports no sizes.
